# Third-Party Notices

This document applies to the standalone AttaLambda distributions
built with Racket CS 9.3. It accompanies, and does not replace, the AttaLambda
`LICENSE`. Third-party components remain governed by their own terms below.

The bundled-code inventory is intentionally based on the executable module
closure and native runtime inputs, not on every package present in the full
Racket development installation. Operating-system libraries listed as dynamic
assumptions in `BUILD-MANIFEST.txt` are supplied by the target operating system
and are not copied into the AttaLambda archive.

